# The clean command hands the frame from step to step: what `load` gives `smooth` takes, what `smooth` gives the plot
# draws, and the figure `draw` makes stays inside `save`, which writes it. The places are made whole at the command: the
# raw file is filled only where it is missing, in an arm, so it stands between the download and the reading.


route sunspots.cli.run
step run/Settings()
choice run/?1
step run/?1/download
step run/?1/download/get                                          # `response = requests.get(..)`
step run/load
step run/load/read_csv                                            # `table = pd.read_csv(..)`
step run/load/to_datetime                                         # `first_days = pd.to_datetime(..)`
step run/smooth
step run/Trend()
step run/Trend.save
step run/Trend.save/Trend.draw
step run/Trend.save/Trend.draw/Figure                             # `figure = Figure(..)`
step run/Trend.save/Trend.draw/add_subplot                        # `ax = figure.add_subplot()`

line entry > run call
line run/Settings() > Settings·settings@run/Settings() value
line Web(www.sidc.be) > run/?1/download own                       # the response is written to the file
line run/?1/download/get > Response·response@run/?1/download/get value
